<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain has no comment on intervention talk.</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain has no comment on intervention talk.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain declined to comment on foreign exchange market talk that it was intervening to brake the peseta's rise.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not make comments (on forex movements),&quot; a spokesman for the Bank of Spain said.</p>
<p>Earlier, the peseta broke resistance at 84.00 per mark, reaching its strongest level since May.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
